Own each MFC engine in its SPU context. A fixed eight-slot registry retained
stopped transient contexts, then shared one fallback engine between unrelated
jobs and acquired a global lookup lock on every channel access. Context-owned
storage keeps queue and tag state independent without a global limit or lock.
Place it before local-store storage so selective SPURS job resets clear it.

